    "note": [
     {
      "text": "66-year-old female presenting with excessive thirst and frequent urination for 3 weeks. Character: passing urine many times, also at night; radiation: n/a; aggravated by sweet food; relieved by nothing. Severity 9/10. Associated: weight loss, tiredness. PMH: Type 2 diabetes for 11 years; Hypertension for 5 years. Drugs: Metformin 500 mg; Amlodipine 5 mg. Allergy: peanuts. Family: asthma. Personal: chews tobacco. Triage: URGENT."
